%% 14-runbooks-syncconflict — a Syncthing conflict in the workspace.
%% Source of truth: src/14-runbooks-syncconflict.mmd. Generated outputs are never hand-edited.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    %% atlas-participant L linux-mint
    participant L as workstation
    %% atlas-participant S syncthing
    participant S as syncthing
    %% atlas-participant E obsidian
    participant E as operator workspace
    %% atlas-participant A github-copilot
    participant A as Agent
    %% atlas-participant Y linux-mint
    participant Y as User

    L->>S: edit note
    E->>S: agent appends to the same note
    S-->>E: cannot merge
    S->>E: writes <name>.sync-conflict-<date>-<device>.md
    A->>E: session start — check for conflicts
    alt conflict file present
        A->>Y: STOP and report the filename
        Note over A: never resolve a sync-conflict file silently,<br/>never delete either side
        Y->>E: reconcile by hand
    else clean
        A->>E: proceed — append only
    end
    Note over A,E: why appends: two devices editing<br/>whole-file rewrites is what creates conflicts.<br/>Appending rarely collides.
    A->>E: never touch .obsidian/ .trash/ .stfolder Archive/ *.bak*
